   "n_tokens": 180,
   "text": "When the electrode touches the workpiece, a short circuit is created [fhwa-hif-19-088:p67:c1]. The arc is extinguished [fhwa-hif-19-088:p67:c1]. The current increases dramatically, superheating and melting the electrode [fhwa-hif-19-088:p67:c1]. The electrode breaks the short and initiates a momentary arc [fhwa-hif-19-088:p67:c1]. A small amount of metal is transferred to the work [fhwa-hif-19-088:p67:c1]. This cycle repeats between 20 and 200 times per second [fhwa-hif-19-088:p67:c1].",
