   "total": 1.0,
   "correct": true,
   "n_tokens": 156,
   "text": "Mixing fine-textured dredged material (silt and clay) with coarse-textured marginal soil (sand) to adjust the texture to approximately a loam soil improves physical and chemical characteristics for crop production [usace-em-1110-2-5025:p511:c0]. Adjusting the water content of dredged material within the plastic limit range also helps [usace-em-1110-2-5025:p511:c0]. Applying ground agricultural limestone to maintain a pH above 6.5 improves agronomic productivity in dredged material [usace-em-1110-2-5025:p510:c1].",
